{
  "maturity": "initial",
  "focalEvent": {
    "label": "Loss of instrument air pressure in RHOB area during maintenance preparation",
    "detail": "At ~10:00 AM, RHOB reported an 'air-low' indication and requested Utilities attendance. Work paused at ~10:02 AM before formal boundary release was signed off for WO-527.",
    "status": "unknown","sourceIds":["incident-description","structuredIncident"],"specialistIds":[]
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Utilities air gallery serves RHOB process area and distributes instrument air to the receiving header H-R.",
      "detail":"The directory identifies RHOB as a local area name for records, not an individual compressor. The gallery supplies 1SC dryer group D-101 and routes air to RHOB.",
      "status": "supported",
      "sourceIds":["b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Local indication P-R at RHOB receiving header H-R normally shows normal pressure band.",
      "detail":"The point register maps AL-44 to the receiving-header pressure condition. Normal operation implies a 'normal band' reading before 10:00 AM (6.8 bar).",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1","da0260c0-7d49-43e8-b074-da2a14c7d59c#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Pressure upstream of distribution routes (P-U) remained stable at 6.9 bar during the event window.",
      "detail":"Measurements show P-U was constant at 6.8–6.9 bar from 09:54 to 10:08, indicating supply pressure did not drop significantly upstream of RHOB.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["fcd254db-75b3-4a9d-abec-44c5b6a9b34e#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Maintenance acceptance signature was not yet signed at notification time.",
      "detail":"The work package cover explicitly states 'Maintenance acceptance signature: not yet signed' when the incident occurred, meaning formal boundary release had not been granted.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"No line opening was authorized at the time of interruption.",
      "detail":"Shift log entry at 10:02 AM explicitly records 'No line opening authorized' while work was paused and issue under review.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Area directory does not establish valve positions or pressure availability at any given time.",
      "detail":"The area and service directory is a location index only; it explicitly states it 'does not establish valve positions or the pressure available at any given time.'",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Desk entries do not log every field operation or identify the point of interruption.",
      "detail":"The shift log excerpt states 'desk entries do not log every field operation' and explicitly notes they 'do not identify the point at which the air supply was interrupted.'",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"No documented confirmation of understanding regarding root cause assessment or response steps is present.",
      "detail":"Evidence shows no interview concerning fatigue, workload, intent, or discussion confirming how the interruption was handled beyond pausing work.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"event",
      "label":"RHOB reported an 'air-low' indication and requested Utilities attendance at ~10:00 AM.",
      "detail":"Shift log records RHOB entry stating 'Air-low indication. Local controls showing supply complaints. Requested Utilities attendance.'",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"event",
      "label":"Utilities acknowledged receipt of the issue at ~10:02 AM and paused work.",
      "detail":"Shift log records Utilities entry stating 'Work paused. RHOB service issue under review.' following RHOB's request for attendance.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"event",
      "label":"Local indication P-R dropped from 6.8 bar to below alarm threshold (5.0 bar) between 10:00 and 10:03 AM.",
      "detail":"Pressure samples show P-R at 6.8 bar at 09:54, dropping to 5.8 bar at 10:00:11, then 4.1 bar at 10:00:40 (below AL-44 alarm threshold of 4.5 bar).",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["fcd254db-75b3-4a9d-abec-44c5b6a9b34e#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"event",
      "label":"Alarm AL-44 triggered at 10:00:32 and was acknowledged by Utilities.",
      "detail":"Pressure samples show P-R below alarm threshold starting at 10:00:11. Alarm journal shows occurrence time of 10:00:32, acknowledgment at 10:03:14.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["fcd254db-75b3-4a9d-abec-44c5b6a9b34e#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"event",
      "label":"Normal pressure returned at ~10:07 AM after alarm cleared.",
      "detail":"Pressure samples show P-R returning to 6.0 bar by 10:06:20 and normal band (6.8 bar) by 10:06:50. RHOB requested retention of records at this time.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["fcd254db-75b3-4a9d-abec-44c5b6a9b34e#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Crew U-A/U-B had current Utilities operating qualification and energy-control authorization.",
      "detail":"Assignment extract lists both operators with 'Current Utilities operating qualification and energy-control authorization' at shift start.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["7e69d300-c57e-40a8-bb37-35a61073ff33#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Maintenance receiver M-A had boundary acceptance pending.",
      "detail":"Assignment extract lists M-A with 'boundary acceptance pending' status at shift start, consistent with work package cover noting signature not yet signed.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["7e69d300-c57e-40a8-bb37-35a61073ff33#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Work folder WO-527-E was blank at issue time.",
      "detail":"Work package cover attachment index shows 'WO-527-E: Blank at folder issue' for the field execution record, indicating no pre-filled isolation steps or valve states were documented on handover.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    },
    {
      "type":"condition",
      "label":"Daily work briefing topic line read '1SC dryer work and RHOB service coordination'.",
      "detail":"Assignment extract notes the daily briefing attendance sheet contains no valve-by-valve content, only a general topic line.",
      "status": "supported","sourceIds":["7e69d300-c57e-40a8-bb37-35a61073ff33#1"],"specialistIds":[]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "intent":"Identify the physical mechanism causing P-R pressure drop at RHOB.",
      "text":"What specific valve, line break, or upstream disturbance caused the instrument air pressure to drop from normal (6.8 bar) to low (<4.5 bar) in the RHOB receiving header between 10:00 and 10:03 AM?",
      "rationale":"The evidence shows P-U remained stable while P-R dropped, suggesting a localized issue downstream of P-U or within the distribution path to RHOB. Without knowing the mechanism (e.g., closed valve, leak, compressor trip), we cannot determine if it was an equipment failure, procedural error, or external event.",
      "evidenceNeeded":["valve-state-records","alarm-input-mapping","flow-data"],"priority":"high","sourceIds":[],"routedTo":["equipment-tool"]
    },
    {
      "intent":"Determine if the interruption occurred upstream of RHOB's receiving header or within its local distribution.",
      "text":"Was the pressure drop caused by a failure in the 1SC compressor/dryer system (upstream) or by an issue specific to the line serving RHOB?",
      "rationale":"The incident description states 'initial notification does not establish whether the interruption began at the air source, within the distribution system, or at the receiving equipment.' Clarifying this location is essential for root cause analysis.",
      "evidenceNeeded":["piping-diagram","valve-state-records"],"priority":"high","sourceIds":[],"routedTo":["equipment-tool"]
    },
    {
      "intent":"Verify if any isolation or boundary procedures were followed during the interruption event.",
      "text":"Were there documented steps taken to isolate affected equipment or secure boundaries when work was paused at 10:02 AM?",
      "rationale":"The evidence shows 'No line opening authorized' but does not confirm whether standard emergency response protocols (e.g., isolating valves, tagging out) were executed. This affects recurrence prevention.",
      "evidenceNeeded":["emergency-response-logs","isolation-checklists"],"priority":"medium","sourceIds":[],"routedTo":["procedure-planning"]
    },
    {
      "intent":"Confirm whether the alarm input mapping for AL-44 was correctly configured to reflect P-R pressure.",
      "text":"Was the alarm AL-44 ('COMP FAULT') properly mapped to monitor receiving-header pressure (P-R) rather than an unrelated signal like C-11 RUN?",
      "rationale":"The point register states 'PR-12 maps it [AL-44] to the receiving-header pressure condition, not to C-11's trip contact,' but this is a synthetic record. Verification ensures alarms accurately reflect actual conditions.",
      "evidenceNeeded":["alarm-configurations","point-register-revision-history"],"priority":"medium","sourceIds":[],"routedTo":["equipment-tool"]
    },
    {
      "intent":"Assess if the blank field execution record (WO-527-E) contributed to confusion about system state.",
      "text":"Did the absence of pre-filled valve states or isolation steps in WO-527-E lead to miscommunication between RHOB and Utilities?",
      "rationale":"The work package cover notes 'Temporary instruction attachment field: blank.' If this was intended for critical boundary info, its emptiness could explain why no line opening occurred despite the pressure drop.",
      "evidenceNeeded":["work-folder-templates","field-execution-instructions"],"priority":"medium","sourceIds":[],"routedTo":["procedure-planning"]
    }
  ],
  "decision": {
    "summary":"The incident involved a loss of instrument air pressure in the RHOB area during maintenance preparation before formal boundary release. Evidence confirms P-R dropped from normal to low while upstream supply (P-U) remained stable, indicating a localized issue downstream of P-U or within RHOB's local distribution. The interruption occurred without authorized line opening and with no documented confirmation of understanding regarding response steps. Key unknowns include the physical mechanism causing the pressure drop, whether it originated upstream or locally, and if emergency isolation procedures were followed.",
    "evidenceUsed":["fcd254db-75b3-4a9d-abec-44c5b6a9b34e#1","da0260c0-7d49-43e8-b074-da2a14c7d59c#1","b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1","eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078#1","24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1"],"unknowns":["physical-mechanism-of-pressure-drop","location-of-interruption-upstream-vs-local","emergency-isolation-procedures-executed"],"alternatives":["upstream-failure-in-compressor-system","local-valve-closure-or-leak-at-rhob-receiving-header","external-event-affecting-distribution-line-to-rhob"],"confidence":0.75
  },"evidenceRequests":[
    "requestId-1",
    "sourceId:b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1"
  ]}
